WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.460
- You know, we woke up this morning,

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:04.020
and the first thing we
talked about is, like,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.880
wow, it's official, the
Olympic Games are postponed.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.986
What does that mean, what are we gonna do?

00:00:08.986 --> 00:00:12.653
(dramatic electronic music)

00:00:14.922 --> 00:00:19.255
(Yoshiro speaking foreign language)

00:00:25.281 --> 00:00:28.948
(dramatic electronic music)

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.233
- Okay.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.900
- Hello, mate, how's it going?

00:00:35.846 --> 00:00:37.096
- Is that okay?

00:00:41.266 --> 00:00:43.218
- Okay (laughs).

00:00:43.218 --> 00:00:45.420
- Oh, I mean, it's absolutely
the right decision.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.650
- The focus wasn't there,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.360
obviously, the training
facilities weren't there.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.270
Everything, everything
screeched to a halt,

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.460
and it was the time for
us to focus on family,

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:55.390
but you're asking athletes
to prepare themselves

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.410
for the most important
competition of their lives.

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.660
- I think that the best
choice is to do it,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.893
as I said before, the sooner they can,

00:01:04.893 --> 00:01:06.800
but the safer they can.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.310
- We started also to think of,

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.010
if this Olympic Games will be really fair

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.070
if they are seen in July
and August for many reasons.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:18.460
Like, everyone cannot train the same way.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.507
- To be honest, there
was a little part of me

00:01:20.507 --> 00:01:23.500
that's like, oh, thank God, you know?

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:24.620
At least we know, at least now we know.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:26.420
- I know it's the right decision.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:28.820
This is something that's
affecting everybody.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.850
It would put a lot of people's
health and safety at risk

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.553
if it moved forward as planned.

00:01:34.816 --> 00:01:36.097
- How does it make me feel?

00:01:36.097 --> 00:01:38.728
I mean, to be honest, I don't
think it's fully sunk in.

00:01:38.728 --> 00:01:39.650
You know, it's hard to take a little bit.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.140
This was gonna be my last Olympics.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.270
- I started sport when
I was nine years old

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.510
with the goal of eventually
going to the Olympics someday,

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:50.700
and then last year I punched my ticket,

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.260
and I felt like I had

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:55.843
so much to look forward
to going into 2020.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.270
I was on camp in Europe,

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:00.520
away from my husband for three months,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.250
just kind of in the mode where
you put your nerves down.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:06.200
Like, it's the final
sprint towards something

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.418
that you've been working
towards your whole life,

00:02:08.418 --> 00:02:10.835
and (sighs).

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.100
- We were worried they were gonna cancel,

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.360
and if they cancel, for us,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.110
it's like someone just being
like, oh, you know what?

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.550
You go back to the bottom now.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:18.930
You start at the bottom of the mountain.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.440
- My personal frustration
have to be put apart

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.798
for something much more big.

00:02:25.798 --> 00:02:29.465
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.060
Training in the living
room, it's not so easy.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.750
- To fence in the house and the garage

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.370
in a very confined space
is quite difficult,

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.840
and our fencing trainer
is not with us here.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.510
- All have a good kit

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.670
that we were hoping to
use for the Olympics.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.553
It is now in Japan (chuckles).

00:02:49.553 --> 00:02:51.569
- I don't own a treadmill.

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:52.402
I'm on the second floor,

00:02:52.402 --> 00:02:54.100
so I don't think the downstairs neighbors

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.270
would appreciate if I got a treadmill.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:58.760
- We will, over the next
few weeks and months,

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.630
be planning on how, how
we approach the next year,

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.150
the extra year, if you like.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.000
- We're young, we're
lucky we're both healthy,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:09.360
and we kind of both stepped
back and said, okay,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.050
if it doesn't happen now, we
have more time to prepare.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.400
- I'm looking forward to spending
some time with my husband.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.660
There's not really any way
I can isolate away from him,

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:19.810
so he will be spending the next 14 days

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:21.180
on self-isolation with me,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.561
so it'll be nice to have
some quality time together.

00:03:23.561 --> 00:03:27.228
(dramatic orchestral music)

